meta {
  name: Import From Person
  type: http
  seq: 22
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/patients/import-from-person
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "personId": "{{crossTenantPersonId}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (data && data.id) bru.setEnvVar("patientId", data.id);
}

docs {
  Reuse a patient that exists at another business: create the caller tenant's own
  `Patient` projection linked to the shared `Person` identity (surfaced by
  Cross-Tenant Lookup). The order then uses the returned `id` as its `patientId`.
  Captures `patientId` from the response.

  ## Body

  - `personId` (required, UUID) — the shared platform identity to reuse. The
    server re-derives every patient field from the `Person`; the client supplies
    only the id.

  ## Behaviour

  - IDEMPOTENT — if the caller's tenant already has an active patient for this
    identity, that patient is returned unchanged (the identity is NEVER
    duplicated).
  - Otherwise a new patient projection is created in the caller's tenant: identity
    fields copied from the `Person`, `branchId` from the active profile, a fresh
    UMID allocated exactly like a normal registration, and the `Person` marked as
    a patient. Audit-logged as a cross-tenant reuse.

  ## Errors

  - `404 PERSON_NOT_FOUND` — no such person (or it has no phone).

  ## Related

  - A plain `POST /patients` on a mobile that belongs to another tenant is
    rejected with `409 PATIENT_EXISTS_IN_OTHER_TENANT` (carrying `personId` in its
    server-side context) — callers must route through this import instead of
    creating a duplicate. The same mobile may still be used for a family member
    (`POST /patients/:id/family-members`).
}
